From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:37:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: list agents under their space in the sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each space in the expanded sidebar (local and multi-machine) lists its
tabs underneath: agents with their state, how long they have been
working or waiting and "· N shells" from the pane's shells token (set
by the shell-count watcher in the patch repo's extras); plain terminals
dimmed and hideable per space; and where a pane works when that differs
from its space. A space collapses to a status summary. Clicking a line
focuses it on release, switching machines if needed; dragging moves the
pane to another space or reorders tabs; its right-click menu renames,
moves or closes.

The section under the spaces lists only agents waiting on the user:
needing input first, then unread finished turns. It sits right under
the spaces list while there is room. A newly attached client keeps the
turns the server reports unread. next_agent/previous_agent cycle the
most urgent group, and focus_agent numbers agents in tree order, across
machines.

Upstream tests for the replaced agent list, sort toggle and fixed
divider, first_snapshot_establishes_an_idle_baseline_without_server_seen_authority,
local_agent_click_can_cancel_a_pending_remote_switch and
switching_machines_preserves_aggregate_agent_scroll_and_visible_rows
assert the old behavior and fail by design.

